00:23:26.060 --> 00:23:28.420
It could be a legacy service
that you have existing.

00:23:28.420 --> 00:23:31.000
And it's not going
to be Istio-enabled.

00:23:31.000 --> 00:23:32.680
And then what we're
going to show here

00:23:32.680 --> 00:23:37.640
is incremental enablement of
MTLS, first in permissive mode

00:23:37.640 --> 00:23:38.660
and then in strict mode.

00:23:43.150 --> 00:23:43.910
All right.

00:23:43.910 --> 00:23:47.050
So we can move over to my
screen so we can start the demo.

00:23:52.790 --> 00:23:53.350
Oh, good.

00:23:53.350 --> 00:23:53.850
OK.

00:23:53.850 --> 00:23:57.010
So for this demo, I'm going
to use the Midwest cluster.

00:23:57.010 --> 00:23:59.950
And so we've switched context
to the Midwest cluster.

00:23:59.950 --> 00:24:02.989
And just to show you
what's in this cluster,

00:24:02.989 --> 00:24:04.030
these are the namespaces.

00:24:04.030 --> 00:24:09.310
So Istio is in fact deployed
in the Midwest cluster.

00:24:09.310 --> 00:24:11.500
And also we have the
Bookinfo application,

00:24:11.500 --> 00:24:13.900
which we were showing
you just on the screen.

00:24:13.900 --> 00:24:16.270
But let's take a look to
make sure what deployments

00:24:16.270 --> 00:24:17.920
are part of Bookinfo.

00:24:17.920 --> 00:24:19.834
And so here you see
there's a client, which

00:24:19.834 --> 00:24:21.250
is the Bookinfo
full client that's

00:24:21.250 --> 00:24:23.230
going to be generating load.

00:24:23.230 --> 00:24:27.130
There are the four services--
the details service,

00:24:27.130 --> 00:24:29.320
the product page service,
the rating service,

00:24:29.320 --> 00:24:34.110
and three versions of the review
service, so we can do Canary.

00:24:34.110 --> 00:24:35.910
And so what we're
going to do is,

00:24:35.910 --> 00:24:39.600
the Bookinfo client is going
to be hitting the product page.

00:24:39.600 --> 00:24:41.919
But remember I told you
there's also a legacy client.

00:24:41.919 --> 00:24:43.710
So let's just take a
look at where that is.

00:24:43.710 --> 00:24:46.070
If we just do kubectl
get deployments--

00:24:46.070 --> 00:24:47.760
there's this legacy
client that's

00:24:47.760 --> 00:24:50.730
not part of the Istio
or Bookinfo namespace,

00:24:50.730 --> 00:24:54.590
and it's also going to be
hitting the product page.

00:24:54.590 --> 00:24:56.870
Let's first just check
to make sure there's

00:24:56.870 --> 00:24:58.390
no policies installed.

00:24:58.390 --> 00:25:00.530
And so let's see if
there's any policies.

00:25:00.530 --> 00:25:02.540
There's no policies.

00:25:02.540 --> 00:25:05.450
And let's also then
get a Grafana dashboard

00:25:05.450 --> 00:25:07.850
so that we can take a
look at the traffic that's

00:25:07.850 --> 00:25:09.600
hitting the product page.

00:25:09.600 --> 00:25:13.975
And so this is the IP address
for the Grafana dashboard.

00:25:13.975 --> 00:25:16.490
And I've already gone
ahead and set that up.

00:25:16.490 --> 00:25:19.790
So here you see that
there's two QPS of traffic

00:25:19.790 --> 00:25:21.000
hitting the product page.

00:25:21.000 --> 00:25:21.690
So here we are.

00:25:21.690 --> 00:25:24.530
We're looking at the Istio
service dashboard in Grafana,

00:25:24.530 --> 00:25:27.920
and we're looking at what's
hitting the product page.

00:25:27.920 --> 00:25:30.770
And at the moment, there's
two QPS of traffic,

00:25:30.770 --> 00:25:33.150
and it's all non-authenticated.

00:25:33.150 --> 00:25:35.090
So there's no client-side
authentication.

00:25:35.090 --> 00:25:38.730
Anybody that hits the product
page will get a response,

00:25:38.730 --> 00:25:40.910
and you know, it's all 200s.

00:25:40.910 --> 00:25:43.820
So now what we're
going to do is we're

00:25:43.820 --> 00:25:48.750
going to turn on permissive
MTLS in the Bookinfo namespace.

00:25:48.750 --> 00:25:52.310
So what that means is, I'm
going to set up this policy

00:25:52.310 --> 00:25:53.330
and then apply it.

00:25:53.330 --> 00:25:55.070
Let's take a look at the policy.

00:25:55.070 --> 00:25:57.560
So the policy is going
to apply to every service

00:25:57.560 --> 00:26:01.940
in the Bookinfo namespace,
and the mode is permissive,

00:26:01.940 --> 00:26:03.370
and Istio mutual.

00:26:03.370 --> 00:26:06.860
So permissive mode means that
