APARNA SINHA: Thanks.

00:39:38.640 --> 00:39:41.130
CHEN GOLDBERG: So we started
with the first principle,

00:39:41.130 --> 00:39:42.950
consistent experience.

00:39:42.950 --> 00:39:46.740
Consistent experience is often
a trade-off with flexibility.

00:39:46.740 --> 00:39:50.070
When you lock things down
to make them consistent,

00:39:50.070 --> 00:39:51.820
you limit your options.

00:39:51.820 --> 00:39:56.080
As an example, you cannot take a
best-of-breed approach when you

00:39:56.080 --> 00:39:58.410
decide to standardize.

00:39:58.410 --> 00:40:00.750
We also heard Jeff talk
about the need of having

00:40:00.750 --> 00:40:04.380
a platform that evolves as
our requirements continue

00:40:04.380 --> 00:40:06.060
to change.

00:40:06.060 --> 00:40:08.600
Cloud Services Platform
breaks this trade-off

00:40:08.600 --> 00:40:13.120
with a fourth design
principle, flexibility.

00:40:13.120 --> 00:40:16.570
Cloud Services Platform is built
on extensible open software.

00:40:16.570 --> 00:40:19.990
It comes with an ecosystem and
a pluggable architecture that

00:40:19.990 --> 00:40:23.350
gives you flexibility, a choice
of solution, and the ability

00:40:23.350 --> 00:40:27.850
to integrate into them
without introducing friction

00:40:27.850 --> 00:40:30.440
in the user experience.

00:40:30.440 --> 00:40:34.040
If something is missing, you
can fill the gap yourself

00:40:34.040 --> 00:40:37.500
without compromising
consistency.

00:40:37.500 --> 00:40:40.420
The platform allows you
to evolve as your needs

00:40:40.420 --> 00:40:42.760
and requirements change.

00:40:42.760 --> 00:40:45.970
We are leveraging Kubernetes
and Istio extensibility

00:40:45.970 --> 00:40:47.680
in the rich ecosystem.

00:40:47.680 --> 00:40:50.560
So you can customize,
evolve, and integrate

00:40:50.560 --> 00:40:53.140
Cloud Services Platform
to better fit your needs.

00:40:56.020 --> 00:40:57.850
With that, I'm super
excited to share

00:40:57.850 --> 00:40:59.620
that we are the
first major cloud

00:40:59.620 --> 00:41:02.710
provider to offer a
production-ready commercial

00:41:02.710 --> 00:41:05.990
Kubernetes application
in the GCP marketplace.

00:41:05.990 --> 00:41:06.970
Yay!

00:41:06.970 --> 00:41:09.420
[APPLAUSE]

00:41:09.420 --> 00:41:12.710
It is developed by
third-party partners.

00:41:12.710 --> 00:41:15.050
Our commercial
Kubernetes app support,

00:41:15.050 --> 00:41:18.280
usage base building,
simplified licensing,

00:41:18.280 --> 00:41:20.830
and easy deployment
to Kubernetes Engine

00:41:20.830 --> 00:41:24.270
on GCP and everywhere else.

00:41:24.270 --> 00:41:26.760
My favorite part about
this announcement

00:41:26.760 --> 00:41:30.090
is that all Kubernetes app
listed in the marketplace

00:41:30.090 --> 00:41:31.540
are Google-vetted.

00:41:31.540 --> 00:41:34.860
That includes vulnerability
scanning and partner agreements

00:41:34.860 --> 00:41:38.380
for maintenance and support.

00:41:38.380 --> 00:41:40.835
This brings the open Cloud
Services Platform ecosystem

00:41:40.835 --> 00:41:42.710
to you wherever you are.

00:41:45.910 --> 00:41:49.120
Cloud Services Platform is
a unique hybrid offering

00:41:49.120 --> 00:41:52.030
that addresses today's
enterprise challenges where

00:41:52.030 --> 00:41:55.120
you are, in the cloud
and on-premises.

00:41:55.120 --> 00:41:59.080
In the session today, we focused
on the core platform services.

00:41:59.080 --> 00:42:01.270
We introduced the
new GKE On-Prem,

00:42:01.270 --> 00:42:05.080
and how it is consistent
with Kubernetes Engine.

00:42:05.080 --> 00:42:07.840
The new GKE policy
management, Istio,

00:42:07.840 --> 00:42:10.900
together with Stackdriver
and the marketplace,

00:42:10.900 --> 00:42:13.480
gives you tools, an
easier way, to manage

00:42:13.480 --> 00:42:17.670
this multi-cluster environment.

00:42:17.670 --> 00:42:20.510
The key principles of
consistent experience,

00:42:20.510 --> 00:42:23.600
